{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1370420-homebrew-minor-templates-the-swarm-overmind-and-infested","id":1370420,"title":"Homebrew Minor Templates: The Swarm (Overmind and Infested)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-25T12:13:38-08:00","id":1370420,"title":"Homebrew Minor Templates: The Swarm (Overmind and Infested)","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">This is a small piece of a homebrew supplement I've been making contemplating hive minds and swarms as minor templates within the Chronicles of Darkness. Putting it here is mainly an exercise in actually putting it out so it can get some feedback for editing before I move on.<br /> it's worth noting that The Swarm itself is malleable. it could be some G-M nanobots, perhaps it's abyssal in nature, or maybe The Bees Have Finally Fucking Had It. whatever it is, it's here, and it's, uh, it's strange.</span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\">The Swarm</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The things in the shadows go deeper. They always go deeper when the light begins to shine on them. As such, gathering anything concrete about them is an exercise in futility. But humanity knows to fear something primal, a match in nature that has never favoured them and will never favour man. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Swarm.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swarms are ancient and archetypical, whenever things too small to be of use alone, band together for their greater protection, purpose, or society, that is the swarm. All over the world, did anyone suspect that bees, wasps, termites, and other assorted insects were alone? Shadow imitates light, and the Swarm mimics its kin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Swarm, The Hive, The Infestation. These are all names given to similar phenomena. Great supernatural hive entities, gestalt consciousnesses, overminds, and hierarchical hiveminds all fit into this category. They\u2019re spread out but have been known to be fiercely competitive in their regions. The nature of the hive is exactly what it sounds like, but its motives, motifs, and aesthetic are inscrutable, and as varied as it\u2019s infestations. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Swarm plants its roots, and the swarm always remembers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Overmind (Minor Template)</span></span></b></span><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>I remember it so clearly.</i></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Being me.</i></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Instead of us.</i></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You were something else once. You remember the feeling deep inside, the desire to keep your individuality, the feeling of being you. That feeling is gone now. You\u2019re more than yourself, you\u2019re them as well now.</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We Not I (\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You\u2019re more than yourself now. Somehow you\u2019ve become more than a single person. You Subborned an existing Overmind and took its place, developed it naturally, or awakened their other bodies through some other means.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For every dot in this merit, the Overmind can claim more bodies for it\u2019s collective. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022) - 3 bodies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022) - 5 bodies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022) - 10 bodies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) - 20 bodies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) - 50 bodies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order to claim a body for their collective, the Overmind must be in the vicinity of a regular human being suffering a breaking point, they may make a reflexive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Composure + Wits]</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> roll to subvert them and add them to your existing bodies. You may control as many bodies at once as dots you have in </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We Not I </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">More Than a Man (\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You may add mental attributes from multiple bodies onto each other for rolls as long as they are in the same scene as each other. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Royal Jelly (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Overmind secretes a \u2018royal jelly\u2019 and may feed this jelly to any infested being under their control. This infested will then become an overmind in its own right while retaining all of it\u2019s infested abilities.</span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Starting as an Overmind:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You start with 2 dots in We Not I and 10 merit dots, as well as 4 integrity.</span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Infested (Minor Template)</span></span></b></span><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Were you one of the lucky ones?</i></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>No, you never were.</i></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You were never one for luck. Now you\u2019re stuck like this. You\u2019re one of the underlings, one of the community, one of the Swarm.</span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infested (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The character is one of the Hive\u2019s Drones, a regular human twisted to serve its will and whims.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The character is now part of a swarm and gains the ability to confer with any other infested individual. Additionally, they can draw on knowledge from another, gaining +1 to all mental skills. This comes at the cost of their free will, however, as they must make a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">composure + resolve</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> test to refuse an order given from the overmind. Additionally, after every order refused, they gain a cumulative -2 penalty on future resistance rolls.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Builder (\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Infested or Overmind</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The process of being Infested has allowed you to produce building material. This could be anything from beeswax, wasp paper, warped iron or something else entirely. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Character can produce this material, making a size 1 object, the sie increasing by one per turn with a corresponding increase in durability.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Pheromones (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Infested or Overmind</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The infested can release a cloud of pheromones into the air allowing them to gain the trust of anyone near the pheromone. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When they are in the physical presence of anyone able to absorb the pheromones, the infested may choose to release a cloud of pheromones that either Decreases the target\u2019s amount of doors by 2 or gives a +2 dice pool to social actions in the scene towards anyone else physically present.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Combat Pheromones (\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Infested or Overmind</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Infested pheromones are tailored for combat.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For three dots, the infested may mark the target as hostile to all nearby infested, making them instantly aware of the target\u2019s location and hostility. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For Five dots the infested gains the ability to roll <b>Composure + Wits - Stamina</b> to instil the Fear, Fatigued or Shaken conditions on the opponent</span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Starting as an Infested:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You start with 3 dots infested and 10 merit dots, as well as 5 integrity.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25117-yackronin","user":"Yackronin","date":". 02-25-2020, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25117-yackronin","name":"Yackronin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}